# ---- /etc ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin/etcfiles, less what Admin/dest routes elsewhere and what has no source.
#
# login and passwd are in binfiles too, and dest tests binfiles first, so both
# go to /bin and are built there, not here.
#
# termcap is not a program: cmd/termcap builds the terminal database with
#     termcap.obj: termcap.src
#     	ed - termcap.src < reorder
# and installs it cp termcap.obj ${DESTDIR}/etc/termcap.
#
# Recovered from the Eighth Edition, staged by ./patch or copied from mk/gen/etc:
# finddev, fstat, rp07dump, rp07rest, install, mklost+found, shutdown and group.
# whoami is the machine name; mtab and utmp are empty, as in v8.
#
# System-specific configuration, in mk/gen/etc, modelled on v8's:
#   ttys      generated from this kernel's own complement -- console, the 32 dz
#             lines four dz11s give, and 64 stream pipes.  The eight lines
#             v10-launch configures carry getty; the rest are present but off.
#   fstab     colon-separated per fstab(5); getfsent takes rw/ro/sw as well as a
#             number, and sw becomes FSSWAP (-2), which mount -a skips along
#             with the / line.  Lists root, /usr, swap and the golden's two.
#   rc        vanilla in shape: fsck on autoboot, then `mount -a', which is what
#             fstab is for.  Only the Interlan and the two netfs mounts are
#             spelled out -- nafsmnt takes a host and a port, and fstab(5) has
#             no field for either.
#   passwd, services, hosts, networks, motd, group
#
# These four faults are repaired in ./patch rather than excluded:
#   gets      taken out of libc on purpose (gets.c-1: "Deleted from libc.a by
#             td, 88.11.07"), so the six call sites use fgets instead
#   tell      absent entirely; tell(f) is lseek(f, 0L, 1)
#   BSIZE     dumprestor.h meant 512, per v8 param.h:96 and the name 512restor
#   sys/tty.h fstat.c includes it and uses nothing from it
#
# fstat is built -O for the reason track and pstat are: -Od2 means as -d2, word
# displacements, and fstat.o overflows them.  Not in Admin/large either.
#
# Superseded, kept for the record:
#   512restor rp07dump rp07rest   call gets(), and v10's libc has none -- its
#                                 mkfile lists fgets.o and ftell.o, not gets.o
#   bad144                        calls tell(), likewise absent
#   restor dumpdir                include <dumprestor.h>, whose line 25 is
#                                 `char c_addr[BSIZE];' while param.h:77 makes
#                                 BSIZE(dev) a macro taking an argument.  That
#                                 header is byte-identical to the r70include
#                                 tape's, so v10 shipped an include tree its own
#                                 param.h contradicts
#   fstat                         needs <sys/tty.h>, which v10 does not have
#
# Still not built, no source anywhere: analyze and catman are 4.3BSD's
# (etc/catman.c and old/analyze.c), and backsh and dklisten appear in no BSD,
# in v10's own manual, or anywhere in the corpus but etcfiles.  Former list: analyze, backsh, catman, dklisten, finddev, fstat, group, install, mklost+found, motd, mtab, rp07dump, rp07rest, shutdown, ttys, utmp, whoami.
# group, motd, mtab, ttys and utmp are data files -- the only copies anywhere
# are under history/ix/root/etc, which is IX, a different operating system, and
# excluded.  The rest have no source at all; the names that appear to match are
# other things (libc/sys/fstat.s is the syscall stub, whoami.h is pascal's,
# install.asd and lcc/doc/install.ps are unrelated).




